There's nothing wrong with basing features on real life; that's
where people draw their experiences from and so that's how you
follow a principle of least surprise.  (It's not really real life;
it's matching player's expectations -- which sometimes isn't the
same thing.)

As a general rule, gameplay should be the first concern, and matching
player's expectations should be a second concern.  My suggestion
is really based primarily on the first.

